   "id": "mICKhyvdBgAJ",
   "from": "Seongho Bae",
   "author": "6a75f6f91a59c568",
   "date": "2017-10-04T14:26:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: What's the item remove standard based on h2?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">In many cases, the rule of thumb of item selection have followed the tradition of structural equation modelling, that is not fit well with MIRT theories.<div><br></div><div>The basic of item selection rule may be present three parts: check model SE reached local maximum, check item fit and combinate items using item information (xxIRT package may help you). But that is not always &quot;standard&quot;, so that You may have to learn IRT basics and psychometric theories.</div><div><br></div><div>Moreover, statistical indices are not crucial than item quality like readability, differential item functioning by SES (Social-Economic Status), Adverse Impact for disability, etc. Statistical indices just help you can find out the test can be fair. HTH.</div><div><br></div><div>Seongho<br><br>2017년 9월 9일 토요일 오전 12시 7분 10초 UTC+9, jeremy keller 님의 말:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">What standard do you use to decide whether to remove item?<br><br>在 2017年9月8日星期五 UTC+8下午10:18:52，Phil Chalmers写道：<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Don&#39;t use this standard, it&#39;s arbitrary. </div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Phil</span><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Sep 8, 2017 at 3:58 AM, jeremy keller <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">778...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Call</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df_core</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df_core_mirt_model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> itemtype </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;graded&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MHRM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Full</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">information item factor analysis </span><span style=\"color:#008\">with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Converged</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> within </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.001</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tolerance after </span><span style=\"color:#066\">69</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> MHRM iterations</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mirt version</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.24</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>M</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">step optimizer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NR1</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>I will get the result like:</div><div><div>q02 0.0000 0.000 0.672 0.000 0.000 0.45192</div><div>q03 0.0000 0.000 0.000 0.000 0.373 0.13939</div><div>q04 0.2339 0.000 0.000 0.000 0.000 0.05470</div></div><div> The h2 value is 0.45192,0.13939,0.05470.</div><div>item should be removed if h2 is low, What&#39;s the experimental standard?</div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;mirt-package&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">mirt-package...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1